WEBVTT

00:01.690 --> 00:04.960
<i>It's been a few days since 
the incident at school.</i>

00:04.960 --> 00:06.860
<i>Today is a day off.</i>

00:08.490 --> 00:10.030
Sh-Shrimpy-san...

00:10.030 --> 00:12.930
Are you sure I don't look weird in this outfit?

00:14.450 --> 00:15.910
I think you look perfectly fine.

00:15.910 --> 00:18.660
P-Please don't poke your head out so much!

00:18.660 --> 00:21.280
People will realize that I'm Shy!

00:21.280 --> 00:25.170
Unbelievable. I only came along because 
you were nervous and asked me to.

00:25.430 --> 00:30.300
Well... i-i-it's been so long 
since I went out with a friend.

00:32.220 --> 00:33.470
Hey!

00:33.470 --> 00:35.180
Momijiyama-san!

00:35.710 --> 00:37.680
Sorry! Have you been waiting long?

00:38.440 --> 00:40.750
No! I just got here.

00:40.750 --> 00:42.810
Really? That's good.

00:43.390 --> 00:46.700
And you must be the Shrimpy-san that 
I keep hearing about. Nice to meet you.

00:46.700 --> 00:47.570
Pleasure.

00:50.470 --> 00:55.220
K-Koishikawa-san, are you 
sure your leg is okay?

00:55.990 --> 01:00.040
Yeah! Check it out! 
It doesn't hurt at all anymore!

01:00.040 --> 01:03.580
I had it checked, and the doctor said 
it's fine. Nothing's wrong with it.

01:03.970 --> 01:06.930
Though they did say it's
unusual that it's fine now.

01:08.550 --> 01:11.960
<i>According to Shrimpy-san, 
Koishikawa-san's leg</i>

01:11.960 --> 01:15.580
<i>might've gotten better due to 
a side effect from the ring.</i>

01:16.050 --> 01:19.310
<i>We're currently awaiting more details.</i>

01:19.310 --> 01:20.700
Momijiyama-san!

01:22.560 --> 01:26.060
<b>Additional shows added!!</b>

01:22.910 --> 01:26.060
Come on, let's go! I want 
to thank you properly today.

01:26.870 --> 01:30.060
By the way, that outfit's really cute on you!

01:30.060 --> 01:31.190
Huh?!

01:33.370 --> 01:34.830
Fank you very mush!

03:05.950 --> 03:12.670
<b><u>Episode 3
</u>Conversation at
the Dinner Table</b>

03:16.870 --> 03:19.620
Man, this is fun!

03:19.620 --> 03:24.430
It's been so long since I've been able to walk 
around freely like this. It's super fun!

03:26.810 --> 03:28.430
Are you having fun?

03:29.190 --> 03:32.270
Y-Yup... Having lots of fun...

03:32.270 --> 03:33.690
Momijiyama-san?!

03:33.690 --> 03:35.080
Wh-What's wrong?

03:35.080 --> 03:36.570
Nothing. It's just...

03:37.710 --> 03:42.200
Teru ends up feeling unwell when 
she does lively activities like this.

03:42.200 --> 03:43.950
Really?!

03:42.200 --> 03:43.950
<b>Shock</b>

03:43.950 --> 03:48.400
I'm an indoor person. 
In other words, I'm a shut-in...

03:48.400 --> 03:49.950
A shut-in?!

03:48.450 --> 03:49.950
<b>Indoor person
(Shut-in)</b>

03:50.290 --> 03:52.720
S-Sorry. Why don't we rest a bit?

03:52.720 --> 03:54.280
Sorry about this...

03:56.660 --> 04:02.680
I really had no idea that
you were the indoor type.

04:02.680 --> 04:07.220
I'm sorry. All this because I'm
an indoor person... a shut-in.

04:07.600 --> 04:11.730
I'm really sorry. I wanted to 
thank you for everything today...

04:12.630 --> 04:18.230
<i>O-Oh, no. I'm letting Koishikawa-san 
down because of my creepy condition.</i>

04:19.720 --> 04:22.740
<i>I need to bring up something 
to make her laugh.</i>

04:23.140 --> 04:28.490
B-By the way, when I went back to the 
nurse's office, it was totally d-demolished...

04:28.730 --> 04:31.780
R-Remember when I said, "A bear 
came in!" and they believed me?

04:30.540 --> 04:34.500
<b>Uh...</b>

04:30.540 --> 04:34.500
It went raaawr

04:30.870 --> 04:34.500
<b>Bear</b>

04:31.780 --> 04:33.880
W-W-W-W-W-Wasn't that hilarious?

04:34.500 --> 04:38.960
The nurse's office... That's 
right... I destroyed it...

04:40.590 --> 04:44.400
There was an alert for an imaginary bear 
all throughout town because of me...

04:44.400 --> 04:46.390
No! That's not it! Um...

04:46.630 --> 04:49.270
<i>Don't try to get laughs when
you suck at talking, you dummy!</i>

04:49.270 --> 04:52.020
<i>I always do this!</i>

04:52.020 --> 04:53.610
<i>I just want to disappear.</i>

04:53.610 --> 04:56.520
<i>I want to vanish and become the wind...</i>

04:57.460 --> 04:59.880
You're amazing, Momijiyama-san.

05:01.820 --> 05:03.500
You're the same age as me,

05:03.500 --> 05:06.440
but you've been through things like what 
happened the other day so many times.

05:06.440 --> 05:09.340
You've saved so many people 
and faced danger head-on.

05:10.530 --> 05:11.540
I admire you so much.

05:11.870 --> 05:13.250
H-Huh?!

05:13.250 --> 05:15.900
Wait, you don't need to admire me...

05:17.730 --> 05:22.940
By the way, does anyone 
else know that you're Shy?

05:22.940 --> 05:25.560
No, I haven't told anyone.

05:25.560 --> 05:28.140
Basically just you and the other heroes.

05:28.140 --> 05:30.010
Huh?! Wh-What about your parents?

05:30.640 --> 05:34.450
I mean... it's really embarrassing 
flying around in that outfit.

05:31.390 --> 05:34.020
<b>That outfit</b>

05:34.020 --> 05:37.020
<b>That outfit</b>

05:34.450 --> 05:36.010
I don't want them to find out.

05:36.010 --> 05:39.130
R-Really? I think it's cool.

05:37.020 --> 05:39.520
<b>That outfit</b>

05:40.240 --> 05:43.530
But I see... So that makes me...

05:43.810 --> 05:46.740
your only friend who knows 
Shy's true identity!

05:46.740 --> 05:48.530
That is what that means, right?!

05:50.200 --> 05:53.490
You know... that's really awesome!

05:53.900 --> 05:56.150
U-Um... Koishikawa-san?

05:56.150 --> 05:58.680
Oh, uh, never mind...

06:06.160 --> 06:07.470
A little boy?

06:07.470 --> 06:10.950
Oh, dear. What's the matter, kiddo?

06:10.950 --> 06:14.840
I can't find my mom and dad.

06:14.840 --> 06:15.830
Ah...

06:15.830 --> 06:17.630
That happens all the time.

06:17.630 --> 06:19.260
It does?

06:19.260 --> 06:22.820
You bet. This is pattern 27.

06:23.260 --> 06:26.390
The key to solving this problem 
lies within your Zweihänder!

06:26.390 --> 06:28.070
His Z-Zweihänder?!

06:28.380 --> 06:30.220
My Zweihänder?!

06:30.220 --> 06:31.820
What's a Zweihänder?

06:32.340 --> 06:34.830
This is a Zweihänder!

06:34.830 --> 06:35.980
Shrimpy-san?!

06:36.660 --> 06:40.270
All right, kiddo. Let's go on an 
adventure to find your parents!

06:40.270 --> 06:41.170
Okay!

06:41.170 --> 06:42.210
Zwei...

06:42.760 --> 06:46.210
Sorry, Momijiyama-san. 
Let's take a little detour.

06:46.210 --> 06:47.710
Oh, sure.

06:48.140 --> 06:50.530
Let me know as soon as you see them.

06:50.530 --> 06:51.720
Okay, I will.

06:52.450 --> 06:56.470
You're really good with 
kids, Koishikawa-san.

06:57.200 --> 07:00.980
You think so? I wonder if it's because I've 
been taking care of my little brother.

07:01.450 --> 07:05.820
Oh, yeah! My little brother said 
you saved him at the T-1 Hotel.

07:06.350 --> 07:08.340
Thanks, Momijiyama-san!

07:09.810 --> 07:12.930
Heroes really are amazing.

07:12.930 --> 07:15.580
Er, it's really not a big deal...

07:16.210 --> 07:19.020
But I wonder where this kiddo's parents—

07:19.670 --> 07:20.720
Over there!

07:22.920 --> 07:24.640
Hey!

07:26.030 --> 07:28.050
Where were you? We were so worried.

07:26.030 --> 07:28.050
Honestly...

07:28.050 --> 07:30.370
That got resolved faster 
than I thought it would.

07:30.370 --> 07:32.910
Okay, Momijiyama-san! 
Let's go to our next spot!

07:32.910 --> 07:34.320
Oh, sure.

07:34.320 --> 07:35.930
Oh, hey!

07:37.340 --> 07:39.440
Thanks for being so nice to me!

07:39.440 --> 07:43.690
Whoa. You've got a good head on your 
shoulders to say thank you properly.

07:44.230 --> 07:48.190
Now, since I know I can rely on you, 
I've got a very important mission for you.

07:48.880 --> 07:52.380
Whether it be your mom 
or dad or anyone else...

07:52.850 --> 07:54.820
Make sure you're nice to them, too.

07:55.280 --> 07:56.830
Think you can do it, kiddo?

07:58.360 --> 07:59.180
Yeah!

08:05.310 --> 08:09.080
Koishikawa-san, I've been thinking 
about this for a while, but...

08:09.080 --> 08:10.960
Man, Momijiyama-san...

08:10.960 --> 08:11.630
Huh?

08:11.970 --> 08:15.890
I did it! I totally said something 
Shy's said in front of Shy!

08:17.000 --> 08:19.640
Oh, man! I'm so embarrassed right now!

08:19.920 --> 08:24.140
But I really thought I should 
tell him that, so I, uh...

08:24.140 --> 08:25.850
It's the same.

08:25.850 --> 08:26.480
Huh?

08:26.960 --> 08:31.200
Earlier, you said that you admired me...

08:31.200 --> 08:36.200
But I admire you, too, since you didn't 
even hesitate to help that little boy.

08:37.590 --> 08:39.980
Heroes and normal people are the same.

08:40.490 --> 08:44.000
When you're connecting through kindness, 
it doesn't matter who you are.

08:44.650 --> 08:46.920
You made me realize that, Koishikawa-san.

08:48.400 --> 08:51.260
Oh, I-I'm sorry! I said something weird again!

08:52.010 --> 08:55.060
Wow... I've been talking a lot today.

08:56.150 --> 08:59.840
Okay, let's get going! We definitely 
haven't had enough fun yet.

08:59.840 --> 09:01.830
Oh, sure. Let's go.

09:07.960 --> 09:10.320
Look, Momijiyama-san.

09:10.910 --> 09:12.990
It's a poster of Stardust.

09:14.150 --> 09:16.800
Have you ever met him?

09:16.800 --> 09:18.660
No, I haven't.

09:18.660 --> 09:21.260
A rock star and a hero.

09:21.260 --> 09:25.250
I guess he's the only hero who's publicly 
revealed his name and true identity.

09:26.730 --> 09:29.900
He's donated over five billion dollars 
to charitable organizations.

09:29.900 --> 09:34.740
He's established international relief groups,
and his songs comfort so many people.

09:34.740 --> 09:38.680
The number of people he's indirectly 
saved is more than any other hero by far.

09:40.230 --> 09:42.000
Y-You seem to know a lot about him.

09:42.000 --> 09:45.040
Oh, I just happened to 
read all this in a book.

09:46.290 --> 09:51.650
I figure he's also someone who's 
caring and overflowing with kindness.

09:51.650 --> 09:53.110
Probably.

09:53.920 --> 09:56.610
Teru, you've got a call from Spirit.

09:56.610 --> 09:57.360
Huh?

09:59.740 --> 10:03.120
<i>Hello, Teru-chan! It's me, Spirit.</i>

10:03.120 --> 10:05.470
<i>From Russia with love!</i>

10:05.470 --> 10:06.620
Phone call?

10:06.620 --> 10:10.200
Oh, um... Another hero is calling me.

10:10.200 --> 10:14.570
<i>Unilord is summoning you. 
Bring your friend, too.</i>

10:14.570 --> 10:15.440
Huh?

10:15.440 --> 10:17.550
<i>You'll be heading to the 
spaceship we went to before.</i>

10:17.550 --> 10:18.880
<i>I'll be going, too.</i>

10:18.880 --> 10:20.640
Is it important?

10:21.230 --> 10:24.870
You and I have been invited to outer space.

10:24.870 --> 10:26.280
Say what?!

10:26.280 --> 10:30.750
<i>Oh, and I guess Stardust 
will be there this time, too.</i>

10:30.750 --> 10:33.480
S-Stardust, too? Um...

10:34.220 --> 10:38.800
U-Um... What's he like? I, uh...

10:38.800 --> 10:42.740
<i>Ah, you're living up to your name, 
I see. You'll be fine, jeez!</i>

10:45.410 --> 10:53.520
Well... He's very good with words, decisive, 
super confident, and charismatic.

10:53.520 --> 10:58.220
He's charming, a great singer, 
and very good with his words...

10:57.340 --> 10:59.650
<i>Um... Are you drunk?</i>

11:00.910 --> 11:03.660
You know, if I had to 
compare him to something...

11:06.390 --> 11:08.050
I'd say he's a psychopath.

11:11.190 --> 11:12.620
And cut!

11:16.530 --> 11:17.440
Wow...

11:17.970 --> 11:20.570
Your newest album is the best.

11:20.570 --> 11:23.680
That's making this music 
video shoot incredibly fun.

11:23.680 --> 11:25.210
You think so?

11:25.210 --> 11:26.830
I wonder if we got the right flow.

11:27.230 --> 11:28.840
Want to go out tonight?

11:28.840 --> 11:32.410
Well, I'd love to...

11:32.410 --> 11:33.580
But sorry.

11:34.500 --> 11:39.090
<b>Stardust</b>

11:34.500 --> 11:39.090
<b>Britain's Hero</b>

11:35.340 --> 11:38.140
The flow I'm going with tonight's 
already been decided for me.

11:42.570 --> 11:43.570
Shy!

11:45.470 --> 11:48.970
<u>Real Name: Teru Momijiyama
Nationality: Japan
Likes: Horror movies, natto
A 2nd-year middle school student who's
so shy she could die</u>

11:49.410 --> 11:51.480
Heya! Nice to meet you.

11:51.720 --> 11:52.980
It's Spirit!

11:52.980 --> 11:54.520
H-Hello.

11:54.520 --> 11:56.860
We sure have been seeing each 
other a lot lately, Teru-chan.

11:57.270 --> 11:59.550
This is Iko Koishikawa-san.

11:59.550 --> 12:02.380
I-I'm Koishikawa. It's nice to meet you.

12:02.380 --> 12:05.920
Goodness, aren't you a cutie? Pleasure.

12:05.920 --> 12:08.240
Um... So why am I being summoned?

12:08.750 --> 12:13.240
Teru-chan, you retrieved 
that black ring, right?

12:13.670 --> 12:18.460
That was actually the first time anyone 
retrieved it in its complete form.

12:19.210 --> 12:22.210
You did something pretty amazing, Teru-chan.

12:22.210 --> 12:23.410
The ring...

12:24.730 --> 12:28.470
About that ring... There was this boy and...

12:28.910 --> 12:31.410
There's so much I don't understand.

12:32.310 --> 12:33.480
I bet.

12:34.270 --> 12:35.230
Well, anyway...

12:36.080 --> 12:38.730
Let's get going to our home base.

12:39.360 --> 12:42.370
We'll need you to stay back 
in Japan, Shrimpy-san.

12:42.370 --> 12:45.290
Roger. I'll contact you if anything happens.

12:45.730 --> 12:47.870
U-Um, could I get an answer?

12:56.390 --> 12:57.250
It...

12:57.710 --> 12:59.750
It's the Earth!

13:00.090 --> 13:02.710
M-M-M-Momijiyama-san! 
We can see the Earth from here!

13:01.550 --> 13:02.710
<b>Earth!</b>

13:02.710 --> 13:05.010
Yes! That is the Earth!

13:03.670 --> 13:05.010
<b>Earth!</b>

13:05.210 --> 13:07.900
You two, this way.

13:09.040 --> 13:13.390
Unilord will give you all the details, 
but that boy you encountered, Teru-chan...

13:14.000 --> 13:20.150
We call him "Stigma." He's actually 
been spotted all around the world.

13:20.150 --> 13:23.740
Around the world? But what's he after?

13:24.160 --> 13:29.210
Hm... Apparently he keeps saying that 
he wants to free people's hearts...

13:29.210 --> 13:32.560
But there's really no way 
for us to know for sure.

13:32.560 --> 13:33.810
People's hearts...

13:34.220 --> 13:37.520
But for us heroes, he's our biggest problem.

13:37.520 --> 13:39.730
He's our top priority.

13:41.060 --> 13:42.590
Okay, we're here.

13:43.190 --> 13:45.590
Knock, knock! Pardon us!

13:46.080 --> 13:48.190
Hm, I wonder where Yunicchi is.

13:48.190 --> 13:48.880
Oh?

13:49.650 --> 13:50.880
So you're already here.

13:50.880 --> 13:51.850
Here. Let's go.

13:52.130 --> 13:53.400
Oh, my.

13:53.400 --> 13:55.120
So many Shrimpys.

13:55.120 --> 13:55.850
It's...

13:56.150 --> 13:57.850
It's so homey!

13:57.850 --> 13:59.260
There we go.

13:59.260 --> 14:00.990
Are you making borscht?

14:00.990 --> 14:03.110
I've been obsessed with soups lately.

14:03.680 --> 14:06.710
M-Momijiyama-san, who's that?

14:06.710 --> 14:08.610
Oh, that's...

14:08.610 --> 14:10.160
Please forgive my late introduction.

14:10.990 --> 14:13.770
My name is Unilord.

14:14.480 --> 14:17.540
I'm in charge of supervising heroes.

14:17.540 --> 14:19.170
Supervising heroes?

14:19.810 --> 14:23.150
What you went through must 
have been very scary.

14:23.150 --> 14:26.170
We heroes feel quite responsible.

14:26.880 --> 14:30.160
Right now, since you are Shy's 
friend, we would like to tell you

14:30.160 --> 14:34.930
what we must do for our own sakes and
against the danger facing the world, as well.

14:36.420 --> 14:40.720
But first, let's have a chat over
my soup. I'm very proud of it.

14:40.720 --> 14:41.630
Yes.

14:41.630 --> 14:43.790
Whoo! Let's eat!

14:47.970 --> 14:50.730
Wow, it's actually really good.

14:50.730 --> 14:52.450
Is the secret ingredient soy sauce?

14:52.660 --> 14:55.740
Oh, did you notice? 
It makes the soup much richer.

14:56.430 --> 14:57.520
It does.

14:57.520 --> 14:58.460
Um!

14:58.950 --> 15:00.120
Can...

15:00.120 --> 15:02.500
Can I take a picture?!

15:02.750 --> 15:03.670
Huh?!

15:04.330 --> 15:05.250
Iko-san...

15:05.840 --> 15:10.200
This is a top-secret location, so I cannot 
allow unauthorized photography.

15:10.200 --> 15:11.210
Aw...

15:11.210 --> 15:12.760
So as for photos...

15:13.160 --> 15:15.070
Please take them in the photo booth.

15:15.070 --> 15:16.240
Hurray!

15:16.240 --> 15:17.270
<i>That's a thing?!</i>

15:18.240 --> 15:19.520
Say cheese.

15:19.520 --> 15:21.020
Yay.

15:22.190 --> 15:23.520
Wow.

15:23.920 --> 15:26.680
My brother's going to be 
so jealous when I show him.

15:26.680 --> 15:29.950
Do you like heroes, Koishikawa-san?

15:30.840 --> 15:32.960
D-Do you think that's weird?

15:32.960 --> 15:34.660
Especially since I'm in middle school...

15:34.920 --> 15:38.140
Oh, no! Also, I mean, so am I.

15:38.140 --> 15:40.110
And I'm the one who's dressed weird.

15:40.110 --> 15:43.630
No, no! Th-That's not what I meant!

15:46.850 --> 15:48.030
Be careful.

15:48.030 --> 15:48.740
Huh?

15:49.810 --> 15:51.050
Stardust!

15:51.650 --> 15:53.550
I-It's really him...

15:54.120 --> 15:57.560
Well, I see we're all here now.

16:00.790 --> 16:03.310
Well? What did you want to talk about?

16:03.310 --> 16:05.730
Stigma appeared in Japan.

16:06.230 --> 16:09.480
Thankfully, Shy was able 
to retrieve the ring.

16:09.830 --> 16:12.490
Huh... A complete one.

16:13.030 --> 16:14.500
How'd you pull that off?

16:14.500 --> 16:15.870
Huh? Um...

16:16.090 --> 16:19.110
I heard that ring shows a person's heart...

16:19.110 --> 16:22.640
So I tried to understand 
Koishikawa-san's heart and...

16:22.640 --> 16:24.870
I worked really hard, and suddenly...

16:25.100 --> 16:26.900
Ah, that must be her.

16:26.900 --> 16:29.750
I was wondering why there 
was a civilian here.

16:29.750 --> 16:33.760
Um... So what exactly is that ring?

16:33.760 --> 16:35.590
And what happened to me?

16:37.950 --> 16:42.350
This uses a person's heart as 
an energy source to crystallize,

16:42.350 --> 16:45.850
and turns into a device that 
processes that into immense power.

16:46.810 --> 16:49.370
It uses a person's heart as an energy source?

16:49.370 --> 16:51.520
Is that even possible?

16:51.520 --> 16:57.690
A person's heart is filled with an 
unimaginable amount of power.

16:57.690 --> 17:00.630
Our own rings, the Heart-shift bracelets,

17:00.630 --> 17:03.960
also use people's hearts 
as their energy source.

17:05.520 --> 17:10.860
But this ring forces its way deep 
into the heart of the wearer

17:10.860 --> 17:14.550
and tries to draw out the darkness 
within. It's made from malice.

17:15.860 --> 17:19.680
The first time it was seen 
was in my country a year ago.

17:21.080 --> 17:22.810
I saw it with my own eyes.

17:26.690 --> 17:33.340
That day, he used my friend 
to cause a huge tragedy.

17:37.820 --> 17:42.120
Y-You mean your friend had the ring on?

17:42.120 --> 17:45.210
Correct. Just like what happened to you, Shy.

17:45.440 --> 17:48.890
Um... How did you deal with that?

17:48.890 --> 17:49.500
Hm?

17:50.400 --> 17:51.840
I cut it off.

17:51.840 --> 17:54.510
Cut it off? You mean the ring?

17:54.800 --> 17:55.760
No.

17:58.030 --> 17:58.860
The whole finger.

18:00.700 --> 18:03.600
You seem to still have your fingers,

18:03.940 --> 18:07.100
so you're quite lucky, Koishikawa-san.

18:07.600 --> 18:12.440
Hey, stop that! You're clearly scaring them.

18:13.740 --> 18:17.920
I can understand the civilian being 
scared, but that little hero there, too?

18:17.920 --> 18:20.580
No wonder I was summoned.

18:20.580 --> 18:22.200
What are you talking about?

18:22.610 --> 18:25.660
Unilord, let's get down to business.

18:26.120 --> 18:28.210
What do you want from me?

18:30.820 --> 18:33.890
You are one of the few humans who can act

18:33.890 --> 18:36.890
without mercy for your own sake, 
as well as the world's.

18:37.520 --> 18:39.470
That's why I want to ask you this.

18:40.370 --> 18:42.550
I'd like you to fight Shy.

18:43.530 --> 18:44.180
Wha—

18:44.180 --> 18:47.230
Unilord! What are you talking about?!

18:47.230 --> 18:50.940
Currently, if Stigma were to 
appear in front of her again,

18:51.370 --> 18:53.440
she would be unlikely to survive.

18:53.880 --> 18:56.820
I-In that case, Teru-chan and I will—

18:55.750 --> 18:56.820
There's no point.

18:57.930 --> 19:00.720
You wouldn't be able to fight her seriously.

19:00.720 --> 19:02.620
You've grown too attached.

19:03.560 --> 19:09.080
I don't know if she reminds you of someone
else, but you won't be strong enough.

19:10.320 --> 19:11.960
Stardust, you—

19:11.960 --> 19:12.960
Pepesha-san!

19:13.650 --> 19:15.550
I-I'll give it a try.

19:15.950 --> 19:17.440
Teru-chan...

19:17.440 --> 19:19.510
I've been thinking about this for a while.

19:19.950 --> 19:23.290
The way I am now, am I really a hero?

19:23.760 --> 19:25.760
I always knew I lacked strength.

19:26.320 --> 19:29.280
So... I want to become stronger!

19:29.280 --> 19:33.390
So that I'll be able to save everyone!

19:34.140 --> 19:35.750
Momijiyama-san...

19:35.750 --> 19:37.730
Well, that was certainly cool.

19:38.160 --> 19:40.990
You almost sound like a hero. In that case...

19:41.560 --> 19:46.050
Are you ready to quit 
being a hero if you lose?

19:47.580 --> 19:48.240
Wha—

19:48.240 --> 19:50.270
Don't be ridiculous! That's just—

19:50.270 --> 19:51.530
All right.

19:52.310 --> 19:55.340
I-I'll try to win! I'll do my best!

19:59.920 --> 20:00.920
It's...

20:00.920 --> 20:03.430
<b>Multipurpose Room
Section 3 in Space HQ</b>

20:01.200 --> 20:02.570
It's so big!

20:03.840 --> 20:06.280
Teru-chan, are you sure you'll be okay?

20:06.280 --> 20:07.780
I-I'll be fine.

20:07.780 --> 20:09.820
I'm a hero, too.

20:09.820 --> 20:10.810
Teru-chan...

20:10.810 --> 20:12.640
Shy! Come over here.

20:17.680 --> 20:19.820
<i>I know what I said, but... I'm scared!</i>

20:22.490 --> 20:24.320
Let's go over the rules.

20:25.040 --> 20:29.990
These rings we use... They're 
connected directly to our hearts.

20:30.600 --> 20:34.750
If you keep your heart strong, they'll 
give you the strength you ask for...

20:34.750 --> 20:38.340
But if you feel like you can't fight anymore, 
your transformation will instantly be undone.

20:38.880 --> 20:42.080
Meaning, the one whose transformation 
becomes undone loses.

20:42.080 --> 20:44.840
But that puts you at a great disadvantage.

20:45.600 --> 20:46.340
So...

20:46.720 --> 20:51.600
If you're able to hit me in the face even 
once, we'll count it as your victory.

20:52.110 --> 20:53.850
And you're sure about this?

20:55.660 --> 21:01.440
Wh-Why are heroes going to fight 
like this? What's the point?

21:01.440 --> 21:05.170
Shy has little to no battle experience.

21:05.170 --> 21:09.120
Stardust, on the other hand, is extremely 
experienced with using his heart.

21:09.680 --> 21:14.370
If she is unable to to fight against enemies
far more powerful than her here,

21:14.840 --> 21:18.100
she will be faced with more hardships ahead.

21:22.270 --> 21:24.070
<i>I'm shaking so bad.</i>

21:24.070 --> 21:26.880
<i>This is my first time fighting a hero, too.</i>

21:27.400 --> 21:28.660
Unilord.

21:28.660 --> 21:31.640
If I think things are getting too dangerous, I—

21:30.590 --> 21:31.640
No!

21:32.870 --> 21:36.610
No matter what happens, do not 
interfere until this fight is over.

21:37.550 --> 21:40.380
If you take even one step this way, she loses.

21:40.380 --> 21:42.070
She'll have to quit being a hero.

21:43.150 --> 21:47.940
Shy, once this coin hits 
the floor, the fight begins.

21:48.530 --> 21:49.410
Got it?

21:49.410 --> 21:50.160
Yes.

21:54.250 --> 21:57.420
Momijiyama-san!
Don't push yourself too hard!

22:03.800 --> 22:04.920
Here I go!
